{"title":"Accessibility Engineer Roadmap","role":"Accessibility Engineer","summary":"An Accessibility Engineer designs, develops, tests, and improves digital products so that people with disabilities can use them effectively.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Human-Computer Interaction / Cognitive Computing"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Accessibility Engineer designs, develops, tests, and improves digital products so that people with disabilities can use them effectively."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Software engineering"},{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction (HCI)"},{"text":"UX engineering"},{"text":"Assistive technology"},{"text":"Accessibility standards"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Inclusive design"},{"text":"Front-end development"},{"text":"Mobile/web accessibility"},{"text":"Accessibility automation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The engineer may work on websites, mobile applications, enterprise software, operating systems, design systems, AI products, and hardware interfaces."},{"type":"p","text":"A realistic progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech","Accessibility / Front-End / UX Engineering Intern","Accessibility Engineer / Inclusive UX Engineer","Senior Accessibility Engineer","Accessibility Technical Lead","Accessibility Architect / Principal Accessibility Engineer","Accessibility Engineering Manager / Head of Accessibility"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Typical Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Programming + HCI fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Web/mobile development + accessibility fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"WCAG, assistive technologies + accessibility testing"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Accessibility engineering projects + audits + automation"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"Accessibility Engineer / Front-End Engineer"}],[{"text":"2–5 Years"},{"text":"Accessibility Specialist / Senior Accessibility Engineer"}],[{"text":"5–8 Years"},{"text":"Accessibility Lead / Accessibility Architect"}],[{"text":"8+ Years"},{"text":"Principal Engineer / Accessibility Engineering Manager"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"This is a specialized career, so candidates who combine engineering ability with genuine accessibility expertise can differentiate themselves strongly."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Programming + HCI Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Build competency in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"JavaScript / TypeScript"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Java or C++"},{"text":"HTML"},{"text":"CSS"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For accessibility engineering, HTML, CSS and JavaScript are especially important."},{"type":"h","text":"HCI Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-computer interaction"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Cognitive psychology fundamentals"},{"text":"Usability"},{"text":"User-centered design"},{"text":"Interaction design"},{"text":"Information architecture"},{"text":"Mental models"},{"text":"Affordances"},{"text":"Feedback"},{"text":"Error prevention"},{"text":"User research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how different users interact with technology."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Web & Application Accessibility"},{"type":"p","text":"Become strong in front-end engineering."},{"type":"h","text":"HTML"},{"type":"p","text":"Master semantic HTML:"},{"type":"p","text":"<header>"},{"type":"p","text":"<nav>"},{"type":"p","text":"<main>"},{"type":"p","text":"<section>"},{"type":"p","text":"<article>"},{"type":"p","text":"<form>"},{"type":"p","text":"<label>"},{"type":"p","text":"<button>"},{"type":"p","text":"<footer>"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand why semantic HTML is usually preferable to recreating native controls with generic elements."},{"type":"h","text":"CSS"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Responsive design"},{"text":"Focus states"},{"text":"Contrast"},{"text":"Typography"},{"text":"Layout"},{"text":"Reduced-motion considerations"},{"text":"Responsive interaction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"JavaScript"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DOM"},{"text":"Events"},{"text":"Keyboard events"},{"text":"Focus management"},{"text":"Dynamic content"},{"text":"Form validation"},{"text":"ARIA interaction patterns"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Accessibility Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"This is where the specialization becomes serious."},{"type":"h","text":"Accessibility Standards"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"WCAG"},{"text":"WAI-ARIA"},{"text":"Accessible Name and Description concepts"},{"text":"Keyboard accessibility"},{"text":"Focus management"},{"text":"Semantic structure"},{"text":"Forms"},{"text":"Multimedia accessibility"},{"text":"Mobile accessibility"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to distinguish between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Accessibility requirement","implementation","testing","remediation"]}]},{"heading":"Assistive Technologies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Accessibility Engineer must understand how users actually consume accessible interfaces."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the fundamentals of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Screen Readers"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NVDA"},{"text":"JAWS"},{"text":"VoiceOver"},{"text":"TalkBack"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Input Methods"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Keyboard-only navigation"},{"text":"Switch devices"},{"text":"Voice control"},{"text":"Alternative pointing devices"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Visual Assistance"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Screen magnification"},{"text":"High-contrast modes"},{"text":"Text scaling"},{"text":"Browser zoom"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cognitive Accessibility"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand challenges involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Complex navigation"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Reading comprehension"},{"text":"Time limits"},{"text":"Unexpected changes"},{"text":"Excessive cognitive load"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Professional Accessibility Engineering","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The final year should combine:"},{"type":"p","text":"Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Accessibility Standards"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Assistive Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"UX Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Students should learn to perform complete accessibility audits."},{"type":"h","text":"Example Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Product","Accessibility Requirements","Manual Testing","Automated Testing","Assistive Technology Testing","Issue Classification","Developer Fix","Regression Testing","Accessibility Sign-off"]}]},{"heading":"Core Knowledge Areas","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Target Level"],"rows":[[{"text":"HTML"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"CSS"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"JavaScript"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"TypeScript"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"React"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"HCI"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"UX Principles"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Accessibility Standards"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"WCAG"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"ARIA"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Keyboard Accessibility"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Screen Readers"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Accessibility Testing"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Automated Testing"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Mobile Accessibility"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"Usability Testing"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"User Research"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"Inclusive Design"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"UX Writing"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Web Performance"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Git"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"CI/CD"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Accessibility Automation"},{"text":"Advanced"}]]}]},{"heading":"Accessibility Engineering Concepts","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"1. Perceivable"},{"type":"p","text":"Information must be available through appropriate sensory channels."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Alternative text"},{"text":"Captions"},{"text":"Transcripts"},{"text":"Sufficient contrast"},{"text":"Scalable text"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Operable"},{"type":"p","text":"Users must be able to operate the interface."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Keyboard navigation"},{"text":"Visible focus"},{"text":"Appropriate target sizes"},{"text":"No keyboard traps"},{"text":"Accessible menus"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Understandable"},{"type":"p","text":"The interface should be predictable and comprehensible."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clear labels"},{"text":"Consistent navigation"},{"text":"Useful error messages"},{"text":"Form instructions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Robust"},{"type":"p","text":"Content should work across different technologies and assistive technologies."},{"type":"flow","items":["HTML","Browser","Accessibility Tree","Assistive Technology","User"]},{"type":"p","text":"An Accessibility Engineer needs to understand this chain."}]},{"heading":"Important Tools","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Browser Testing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Chrome DevTools"},{"text":"Firefox Developer Tools"},{"text":"Accessibility Tree inspection"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Automated Testing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"axe"},{"text":"Lighthouse"},{"text":"Pa11y"},{"text":"Accessibility Insights"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Screen Readers"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NVDA"},{"text":"JAWS"},{"text":"VoiceOver"},{"text":"TalkBack"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Development"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"VS Code"},{"text":"Git"},{"text":"GitHub"},{"text":"React"},{"text":"TypeScript"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Design systems"},{"text":"Component libraries"}]}]},{"heading":"Accessibility Testing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The student should understand that automated testing alone cannot establish complete accessibility."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong process is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Automated Testing","Keyboard Testing","Screen Reader Testing","Visual Inspection","Zoom / Text Scaling","User Testing","Issue Prioritization","Remediation","Regression Testing"]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"p","text":"A button may pass an automated checker but still have poor keyboard behavior or confusing screen-reader instructions."},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Automation","manual testing","assistive technology testing is the stronger methodology."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Major Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Accessible React Design System"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a reusable component library."},{"type":"p","text":"Components:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Button"},{"text":"Input"},{"text":"Checkbox"},{"text":"Radio"},{"text":"Modal"},{"text":"Dropdown"},{"text":"Tabs"},{"text":"Accordion"},{"text":"Tooltip"},{"text":"Navigation"},{"text":"Form validation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Every component should include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Keyboard support"},{"text":"Focus management"},{"text":"Semantic HTML"},{"text":"Accessible names"},{"text":"Appropriate ARIA where necessary"},{"text":"Error states"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Accessibility Audit Platform"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a web application that analyzes websites."},{"type":"flow","items":["Website URL","Crawler","Accessibility Checks","Issue Detection","Severity Classification","Accessibility Report"]},{"type":"p","text":"Include categories such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Missing alternative text"},{"text":"Form labeling"},{"text":"Heading structure"},{"text":"Keyboard issues"},{"text":"Color contrast"},{"text":"Missing landmarks"},{"text":"Invalid ARIA"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use existing accessibility engines where appropriate rather than trying to recreate every standard manually."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Accessible E-Learning Platform"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an accessible education platform with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Captions"},{"text":"Transcripts"},{"text":"Keyboard navigation"},{"text":"Screen-reader support"},{"text":"Adjustable text size"},{"text":"Accessible quizzes"},{"text":"Clear focus indicators"},{"text":"Reduced-motion option"},{"text":"Accessible forms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Accessible Mobile Application"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an Android or cross-platform application."},{"type":"p","text":"Test:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"TalkBack"},{"text":"VoiceOver"},{"text":"Dynamic text sizing"},{"text":"Touch targets"},{"text":"Screen orientation"},{"text":"Focus order"},{"text":"Gesture alternatives"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Accessibility Remediation Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Select 5 real-world interface examples and document:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Original Interface","Accessibility Audit","Problems Identified","WCAG / Accessibility Principle","Proposed Fix","Implemented Fix","Before vs After","Testing Results"]},{"type":"p","text":"This creates a strong portfolio for accessibility-focused roles."}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Search beyond the exact title Accessibility Engineer Intern."},{"type":"h","text":"Strong internship targets"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accessibility Engineering Intern"},{"text":"Front-End Engineering Intern"},{"text":"UX Engineering Intern"},{"text":"Inclusive Design Intern"},{"text":"UX Research Intern"},{"text":"Design Systems Intern"},{"text":"Software Engineering Intern"},{"text":"QA Automation Intern"},{"text":"Accessibility Testing Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Particularly valuable companies"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for organizations building:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Enterprise SaaS"},{"text":"Consumer applications"},{"text":"Operating systems"},{"text":"Browsers"},{"text":"Mobile platforms"},{"text":"Financial applications"},{"text":"Government digital services"},{"text":"Healthcare platforms"},{"text":"Education platforms"}]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Role","Relevance"],"rows":[[{"text":"Accessibility Engineer"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Accessibility QA Engineer"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Accessibility Tester"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Accessibility Specialist"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"Front-End Engineer"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"UX Engineer"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Inclusive Design Engineer"},{"text":"Very High"}],[{"text":"Design Systems Engineer"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"UI Engineer"},{"text":"High"}],[{"text":"UX Research Assistant"},{"text":"Medium–High"}],[{"text":"QA Automation Engineer"},{"text":"High"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong front-end engineer with accessibility expertise can transition into accessibility engineering effectively."}]},{"heading":"Employer Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Employer","Important Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Software Product Companies"},{"text":"Front-end + WCAG + automation"}],[{"text":"SaaS Companies"},{"text":"React + design systems + accessibility"}],[{"text":"Big Tech"},{"text":"Engineering + accessibility + assistive technology"}],[{"text":"Financial Services"},{"text":"Accessibility compliance + testing"}],[{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"Accessibility + usability + inclusive design"}],[{"text":"Government/Digital Services"},{"text":"Standards + auditing + accessible UX"}],[{"text":"Consulting"},{"text":"Accessibility audits + remediation + communication"}],[{"text":"Design-System Teams"},{"text":"Components + accessibility + testing"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certifications can strengthen the profile, but practical testing experience is more important."},{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Web accessibility"},{"text":"WCAG"},{"text":"Accessibility testing"},{"text":"Inclusive design"},{"text":"UX"},{"text":"Assistive technologies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should prioritize:"},{"type":"p","text":"Accessibility Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Hands-on Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Real Projects"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Portfolio Evidence"},{"type":"p","text":"rather than collecting many certificates."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A master's degree is not mandatory."},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant PG options include:"},{"type":"p","text":"M.Tech / M.E."},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Computer Science"},{"text":"Software Engineering"},{"text":"Information Technology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"M.Des"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interaction Design"},{"text":"UX Design"},{"text":"Product Design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"M.Sc / M.S."},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HCI"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Computer Science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accessibility / Inclusive Design specialization"},{"text":"Assistive Technology"},{"text":"Cognitive Science"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For technical accessibility engineering, a strong CS/HCI + software engineering background is particularly useful."}]},{"heading":"Career Specializations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"1. Web Accessibility Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HTML"},{"text":"CSS"},{"text":"JavaScript"},{"text":"React"},{"text":"WCAG"},{"text":"Screen readers"},{"text":"Browser accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Mobile Accessibility Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Android"},{"text":"iOS"},{"text":"TalkBack"},{"text":"VoiceOver"},{"text":"Mobile interaction patterns"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Accessibility QA Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Test automation"},{"text":"Manual testing"},{"text":"Regression testing"},{"text":"Accessibility audits"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Design Systems Accessibility Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accessible component libraries"},{"text":"Design tokens"},{"text":"UI standards"},{"text":"Component testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Assistive Technology Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Screen readers"},{"text":"Alternative input"},{"text":"Speech interfaces"},{"text":"Accessibility APIs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Inclusive AI Engineer"},{"type":"p","text":"An emerging path involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI interfaces"},{"text":"Voice interfaces"},{"text":"Multimodal systems"},{"text":"Accessible AI assistants"},{"text":"Bias and inclusion"},{"text":"Human-AI interaction"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Technical Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Accessibility Engineer","Senior Accessibility Engineer","Staff Accessibility Engineer","Principal Accessibility Engineer","Distinguished Engineer"]},{"type":"h","text":"UX Engineering Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["UX Engineer","Senior UX Engineer","Accessibility / Inclusive Design Lead","Principal UX Engineer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Leadership Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Accessibility Engineer","Senior Engineer","Accessibility Technical Lead","Accessibility Engineering Manager","Head of Accessibility"]}]},{"heading":"Emerging Technologies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Accessibility engineering is increasingly affected by:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Generative AI"},{"text":"Multimodal AI"},{"text":"Voice interfaces"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Speech recognition"},{"text":"AI-powered assistive technology"},{"text":"Wearable computing"},{"text":"Spatial computing"},{"text":"AR/VR accessibility"},{"text":"Brain-computer interfaces"},{"text":"Personalized interfaces"},{"text":"Adaptive UX"},{"text":"AI-assisted accessibility testing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A particularly important area is AI accessibility."},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Camera","Computer Vision","Object / Text Recognition","LLM","Natural Language Description","Speech Output","User"]},{"type":"p","text":"Such systems can create powerful assistive experiences, but they also require careful evaluation for accuracy, privacy, reliability, and bias."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Frontend"},{"type":"p","text":"├── HTML"},{"type":"p","text":"├── CSS"},{"type":"p","text":"├── JavaScript"},{"type":"p","text":"├── TypeScript"},{"type":"p","text":"└── React"},{"type":"p","text":"Accessibility"},{"type":"p","text":"├── WCAG"},{"type":"p","text":"├── WAI-ARIA"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Semantic HTML"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Keyboard Accessibility"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Focus Management"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Accessible Forms"},{"type":"p","text":"Assistive Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"├── NVDA"},{"type":"p","text":"├── JAWS"},{"type":"p","text":"├── VoiceOver"},{"type":"p","text":"└── TalkBack"},{"type":"p","text":"Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"├── axe"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Lighthouse"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Accessibility Insights"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Manual Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Automated Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"HCI"},{"type":"p","text":"├── UX"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Usability"},{"type":"p","text":"├── User Research"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Cognitive Principles"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Inclusive Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Git"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"├── CI/CD"},{"type":"p","text":"├── React Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Web Performance"}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, a strong candidate should be able to:"},{"type":"h","text":"Build"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accessible React applications"},{"text":"Accessible component libraries"},{"text":"Accessible forms"},{"text":"Keyboard-friendly interfaces"},{"text":"Responsive interfaces"},{"text":"Accessible mobile applications"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Test"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Websites manually"},{"text":"Screen-reader workflows"},{"text":"Keyboard navigation"},{"text":"Zoom/text scaling"},{"text":"Automated accessibility rules"},{"text":"Accessibility regressions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analyze"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accessibility defects"},{"text":"User journeys"},{"text":"WCAG requirements"},{"text":"UX problems"},{"text":"Cognitive accessibility issues"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Communicate"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should be able to explain:"},{"type":"p","text":"Who is affected, what accessibility barrier exists, why it occurs, how it should be fixed, and how the fix was verified."}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest graduate profile is:"},{"type":"p","text":"Accessibility-focused Front-End / UX Engineer with strong HCI, WCAG, assistive technology and accessibility-testing expertise."},{"type":"p","text":"Not simply:"},{"type":"h","text":"\"I know accessibility standards.\""},{"type":"p","text":"The candidate should demonstrate actual engineering ability."},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["HCI + Cognitive Computing","HTML / CSS / JavaScript","Frontend Engineering","HCI + UX","WCAG + ARIA","Assistive Technology","Accessibility Testing","Accessibility Automation","Accessibility Engineering"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best final positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Frontend Engineering","HCI","Accessibility","Assistive Technology","Automated Testing","Inclusive Design"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination provides a much stronger career profile than treating accessibility as only a compliance/testing function."}]}]}